v 2.7, October 2026 - VASP parser fixes (on-the-fly ML runs, any cell shape) and repair_umd.py; FFT mean square displacements with diffusion errors; viscosity rewritten; vibrations_umd.py and vdos_thermo.py
v 2.8, October 2026 - automated workflow (umd_workflow.py); all the structural scripts for any cell and NPT runs; check_umd.py, build_umd.py; new parsers and converters; thermodynamic integration and full thermodynamics rewritten. In detail:
- gofr_umd.py and bonding_umd.py: one method for any cell shape and for NPT runs; each bond counted once
- analyze_gofr.py: automatic analysis of all pairs, with optional manual correction; replaces three scripts
- speciation_and_angles.py: correct angles in any cell, bond lifetimes, single atoms as species; lifetimes.py and liquid_and_vapor_speciation.py rewritten
- averages.py -a: full thermodynamics with correct energies, heat capacity and errors (replaces fullaverages.py)
- msd_umd.py -a tensor: diffusion tensor and its principal axes
- build_umd.py: supercells, shuffling, insertion, scaling, substitution, removal of molecules, extraction of atoms (replaces build_supercell.py, box_shuffle.py, insert_umd.py, extratom_umd.py); velocities fixed
- check_umd.py: quality checks of a run (replaces check_overlap.py)
- umd2out.py: extended XYZ, LAMMPS data and dump, DeepMD outputs
- LAMMPSParser2umd.py rewritten: any box, NPT, units, thermo output matched by step
- VaspParser.py writes the total electronic (free) energy again
- thermo_integration_umd.py rewritten (Gauss-Legendre quadrature, errors)
- crystallography.py: coordinate conversions correct for any cell
- viscosity_umd.py: the stress autocorrelations in their own file, <base>.stress.scf.dat, also normalized
- umd_processes_fast.py: faster and more robust reader of UMD files; the last snapshot is no longer missed with sampling
- the header of the UMD files ends with a line stating the code that produced the run (origin)
- documentation folder: updated flowchart of the package, and the UMD paper
- umd_workflow.py: automated workflow over UMD files, by panels of the flowchart (-g structural, -t transport, -d thermodynamics), with a summary table
- bonding_umd.py: -i initial snapshot (the bonding file records it for the speciation and the cluster MSDs); the cutoff file is now -c (-i <file> still works)
- msd_umd.py: -i initial snapshot and -s sampling
- msd_clusters_umd.py reads the popul files written with the angles (speciation_and_angles.py -t 1)

v 2.8.1, October 2026 - fix: analyze_msd.py runs as a command (python3 line at the top); quick help of the scripts:
- analyze_msd.py: the first line #!/usr/bin/env python3 was missing, so the shell, not python, ran it when called by its name
- documentation folder: quick help of the scripts (umd-quick-help.pdf)

v 2.8.2, October 2026 - g(r) of selected pairs:
- gofr_umd.py: -c central and -a adjacent elements, the g(r) of these pairs only, in <base>.<central>-<adjacent>.gofr.dat

v 2.8.3, October 2026 - g(r) analysis by clicks and with better minima; former outputs removed when a script is run again:
- a script run again first removes the outputs of its former run on the same input: gofr_umd.py (the gofr file of the same selection; those of other selections are kept), analyze_gofr.py (the .inp files and plots of each gofr file), speciation_and_angles.py (the files of the same -r: -r 0 keeps the r1 files and vice versa), msd_umd.py, vibrations_umd.py, check_umd.py (also the optional outputs: tensor, axes, overlap), msd_clusters_umd.py (the species no longer found), liquid_and_vapor_speciation.py, lifetimes.py, umd2out.py (all the files per snapshot, with -k only that one; the deepmd set); build_umd.py keeps its former builds
- analyze_gofr.py: the .inp files list every pair, 0 (no bond) for the pairs not computed or without a shell
- gofr_umd.py -c/-a: the reverse pairs too (-c O: O-X and X-O), and all the pairs of the system are written, the others with g(r) = 0, so that analyze_gofr.py gives them 0 (no bond)
- analyze_gofr.py: -c central and -a adjacent elements, as in gofr_umd.py (the pairs central-adjacent and their reverse); -a with pairs (-a Si-O,Mg-O) still works
- analyze_gofr.py: the first minimum is a 3rd-order polynomial (formerly a parabola, biased on asymmetric dips), both fits at most 1 A wide; cutoffs and coordination numbers change slightly (pyrolite Si-O 4.06 -> 4.00, Al-O 4.19 -> 4.09)
- analyze_gofr.py -v: buttons Discard, Automatic, Manual input (the automatic fits on the clicked peak and dip), All manual (the clicked points), Previous, Next; two left clicks, maximum then minimum (the right click for the minimum did not work on Mac trackpads); one pass over the pairs, Next on the last pair closes and writes the files; the terminal table once, one line per pair with the coordination numbers of A-B and B-A

v 2.8.4, October 2026 - MSD fits: window set by clicks, fit after the ballistic regime:
- msd_umd.py and analyze_msd.py: the fit of D starts by default at the end of the ballistic regime of each element (local exponent of the MSD below 1.2), no longer at 0; -b / -s as before; <base>.diffusion.dat gives the window of each column; D changes (pyrolite Na 3.1 -> 2.4 x 10^-8 m2/s)
- analyze_msd.py and analyze_msd_clusters.py -v: two clicks on the graph set the fit window of each MSD (start, then end), refitted at once; buttons Automatic (the default window), Previous, Next (one pass); the files are written when the window is closed, diffusivities.txt with the window of each column (8 columns per species)

v 2.9, October 2026 - umd_clean.py; together with 2.8.1-2.8.4: g(r) of selected pairs, g(r) and MSD fits checked by clicks, D fitted after the ballistic regime, former outputs removed when a script is run again:
- umd_clean.py (new): removes the outputs of the package from a folder (-r: and below), to start the analysis afresh; keeps the UMD files, OUTCARs, dumps and every file that is not an output; by default only lists them, -y moves them to a umd_cleaned_<date> folder (to put back if needed), -y --delete deletes them

